# rule_file_corpus.md is NOT ignored: it is a list of public URLs, and every
# figure this project publishes is measured over the files it names. Without
# it the scripts are unrunnable and the numbers unverifiable, which is the one
# standard this project argues for everywhere else.
# corpus/ itself stays ignored — those are other people's files to fetch, not
# ours to redistribute.
/corpus/

# research artifact — regenerated from the seed, not source
/enforceability-worksheet.txt
/.local-notes/

# Local session status — where work last left off. Never committed; it names
# machine state, account details and open decisions, not product history.
# CHANGELOG.md is the record. Convention is global Rule 17.
/local/

# machine-local Claude Code settings (guard hook, absolute paths)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/rules/guardtest.md
